Raise the AImageReader image count for high-reorder MediaCodec streams

mpv's Android GL interop (hwdec=mediacodec with vo=gpu/gpu-next) creates
its AImageReader with maxImages=5. That value bounds how many decoded
frames may be in flight to GL, and therefore how many output buffers the
MediaCodec decoder can hold in the reader's BufferQueue.

Five is too few for streams with a large reorder/DPB depth. On Rockchip
(c2.rk.avc.decoder, rk3588) an ordinary 1080p H.264 stream is reported
with output.delay up to ~21; the decoder can only fetch a fraction of the
output buffers it needs, produces the first frame, then stalls -
"acquireLatestImage failed: -30001" (AMEDIA_IMGREADER_NO_BUFFER_AVAILABLE),
frozen video over continuing audio.

Raise maxImages to 34: it covers the H.264/HEVC maximum DPB (16) plus
reorder and display slack while staying under the BufferQueue's 64-slot
ceiling. Images are allocated lazily as the producer queues them, so
low-DPB streams allocate only what they use and pay nothing extra.

diff --git a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_aimagereader.c b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_aimagereader.c
index 83c2ea87ef..e56e21b49f 100644
--- a/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_aimagereader.c
+++ b/video/out/hwdec/hwdec_aimagereader.c
@@ -154,9 +154,20 @@ static int init(struct ra_hwdec *hw)
         hw->glsl_extensions = es2_exts;
 
     // dummy dimensions, AImageReader only transports hardware buffers
+    //
+    // maxImages caps how many decoded frames may be in flight to GL, which in
+    // turn bounds how many output buffers the MediaCodec decoder can hold in
+    // its BufferQueue. The upstream value of 5 starves decoders whose stream
+    // carries a large reorder/DPB depth: on Rockchip (c2.rk.avc.decoder) an
+    // ordinary 1080p H.264 stream reports output.delay up to ~21 and can only
+    // fetch a fraction of the buffers it needs, so it stalls after the first
+    // frame ("acquireLatestImage failed: -30001", frozen video with audio).
+    // 34 covers the H.264/HEVC maximum DPB (16) plus reorder and display
+    // slack while staying under the BufferQueue's 64-slot ceiling; images are
+    // allocated lazily, so low-DPB streams pay nothing.
     media_status_t ret = p->AImageReader_newWithUsage(16, 16,
         AIMAGE_FORMAT_PRIVATE, AHARDWAREBUFFER_USAGE_GPU_SAMPLED_IMAGE,
-        5, &p->reader);
+        34, &p->reader);
     if (ret != AMEDIA_OK) {
         MP_ERR(hw, "newWithUsage failed: %d\n", ret);
         return -1;
